\label{thm: main 1 intro}
    Let $(X,T)$ be a minimal Floyd-Auslander system.
Then the following statements are equivalent.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $(X,T)$ is non-tame;\label{item: 1}
        \medskip
        \item the set of minimal idempotents $J^{\mathrm{min}}(X)$ is large: $|J^{\mathrm{min}}(X)|>2^{\aleph_0}$;\label{item: 4}
        \medskip
        \item $\Lambda=\{n\in \mathbb N\colon |Q(n)|\geq 2\}$ is infinite.\label{item: 6}
    \end{enumerate}

