Let $(Q,W)$ be a non-degenerate quiver with potential. If $\mathcal{J}(Q,W)$ is finite-dimensional, then it satisfies the stable Brauer-Thrall II' conjecture. In particular, it satisfies the brick Brauer-Thrall II' conjecture.
